+# The temporal response restarts and returns enclosed sound
+
+[definition] This return extends the [recorded temporal contact](2026-09-07_THE_RECORDED_PREIMAGE_FIBRE_CHANGES_THE_CONTINUING_TEMPORAL_RESPONSE.md)
+on `codex/apple-silicon` after `fb36d505`. The active AS4–AS5 goal continues. This record concerns
+response persistence, complete-recording continuation and the exterior sound receiver; it does
+not assert an acoustic model, English capability, a physical room inverse or streaming completion.
+
+## Native construction and durable boundary
+
+[established-bounded; source-inspected] `ResidentTemporalConditionRest` retains the initial
+rational point, its actual dyadic lift and every chronological compact contact report, including
+cut, response chart, grain, metric and lineage. The existing exact cold decoder continues to
+reconstruct the response from the previous response and the saved Gram/cross moment. Remount
+installs those completed sections into a new move owner; it does not recompute a centre, replay
+a contact, recreate a source capability or require an archive of every waveform.
+
+[definition] The report wire retains the six numerical balls for prior, V, U, successor,
+returned response normal and response difference; two signed residual vectors with their
+positive integer denominators; and the exact G, raw cross moment, px, py and cden. The rest
+validator treats residual denominators as integer denominators, never as ball radii. For
+`A_num = G + cden I`, numerical scale `s = 2^grain` and stored centres Uhat/Vhat, it checks
+`RU = py A_num Uhat - px raw s` and `RV = A_num Vhat - cden priorhat` exactly. It checks the
+native directed radius formulas, the complete ball algebra and exact cold response containment.
+
+[established-bounded; source-inspected] Cold validation also checks the initial lift,
+positive-semidefinite complex Gram realification, the cross moment's compatible range, and
+reduced source/observation denominator constraints. This validates the saved construction's
+algebra. Its origin in a particular recording remains a source-qualified experimental claim;
+file hashes protect the exterior wire and do not identify native holons.
+
+## Public application and sound
+
+[established-bounded; source-inspected] `holonics-hna::native::temporal_acoustic` owns one
+continuing response and exterior recording/contact chronology. Complete source and observation
+charts use their original PCM clock. It predicts before mounting the observation, composes the
+existing comparison and temporal Preimage Fibre, stages the complete native contact, and only
+then publishes its successor and chronological receipt. The callback borrows the prediction,
+difference, unexplained return and both normal currents. Callback failure does not rewind a
+completed contact; the live owner remains available for checkpoint publication.
+
+[definition] The public workbench commands are `holonics-acoustic temporal start`, `continue`,
+`predict` and `inspect`. Checkpoints contain response construction and recording metadata,
+not raw recordings or a complete acoustic ecology. Inspection reports saved exterior provenance;
+it does not re-open every historical recording. The command's output report presents prediction
+sound and contact/work receipts. The SDK callback retains the full recording-relative return
+while in scope; its waveform legs are not silently claimed to be in the response checkpoint.
+
+[established-bounded; source-inspected] `NativeAcousticEnclosedTemporalPcm16Projection` reuses
+the existing exact quantizer and WAV writer. One complex coordinate becomes a two-channel PCM
+frame. The public record calls it a numerical representative and retains one global Euclidean
+radius across both quadratures and all frames. If c is the representative and g is positive
+output gain, each exact quotient remainder satisfies `g c = PCM + remainder`; the entire
+remaining numerical error has global radius `g r` in PCM units. Reconstructing the record
+returns the complete original ball. WAV alone carries its PCM representative, not the ball or
+quantization remainder. Neither codec selection nor hearing the representative asserts that
+the native current was an exact centre or that the compatible cause fibre was a singleton.
+
+[definition] PCM ingestion uses divisor 32768. Output gain is separately declared by `--gain`;
+it does not redefine ingestion or assert calibrated pressure/SPL. The four response taps and
+grain 72 in the recorded comparison remain explicit study declarations. The response is used
+to predict a recording; an arbitrary second utterance is not supplied as an impulse response.
+
+## Verification and measurements
+
+[established-bounded; measured] The [portable return](2026-09-07_temporal_acoustic_application/)
+contains application reports, comparison receipts, observer controls, the one-contact and
+three-contact response checkpoints, measured costs and the later produced WAV. Full per-frame
+PCM reconstruction receipts remain recoverably under
+`.local/experiments/temporal-acoustic-application/`; their hashes and byte populations are in
+the portable comparisons. The largest receipt is 152,454,871 bytes. The WAV in this record is
+only its declared presentation; its complete numerical/reconstruction fibre remains in that
+local receipt and the native response/source construction.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] The public application received the same three complete
+SoundCam loopback/microphone-00 pairs as the preceding verified native return: 672,000 mono
+PCM16 frames per source, 48 kHz, 14 seconds, original zero-origin recording clocks. An
+uninterrupted process and an actual one-plus-two-recording process sequence return identical
+17,926-byte final checkpoints, all three 2,688,056-byte stereo WAVs, and all three complete PCM
+reconstruction receipts. Each saved native contact section is byte-identical to the preceding
+source-qualified report. The new observer explicitly uses that previously validated evidence
+as its reference; it does not present a repeated check as a new universal statement.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] The later `predict` command consumes only the saved response
+and row-000 excitation; it opens no observation input and performs no condition update. Its
+672,003-frame output retains the three-sample causal tail. An independent exact convolution
+of the final rational response and original PCM lies inside the complete output ball, with
+radius `165545277/2361183241434822606848` in native units. Every PCM coordinate, exact remainder,
+clipping flag, receiver, lineage and clock passes comparison. No output coordinate clips at
+this declared gain. This is a target-free application return on previously used source material,
+not a held-out sound-quality or English-capability claim.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] On the M1 Pro, in the development build, the buffered first
+recording takes 53.39 seconds and the subsequent two-recording process takes 212.83 seconds,
+including cold output and checkpoint publication. The continuing native response/constructions
+occupy 14,544 bytes; peak native residency is 392,470,932 bytes. Remount after one contact takes
+0.0284 seconds and ingresses 5,136 bytes; remount after three takes 0.1072 seconds and ingresses
+14,544 bytes. Both enact zero native deeds and zero numerical readouts. These are cold mounts;
+they do not claim zero transfer.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] The two continued native contacts take 26.82 and 27.04 seconds;
+each uses six deeds with zero hot numerical readout/ingress and 384 bytes of receipt egress.
+Later target-free prediction takes 4.35 seconds, one deed, zero numerical readout/ingress and
+64 bytes of receipt egress. Its explicit cold PCM boundary takes 75.24 seconds. Earlier cold
+exports in the buffered sequence take 17.42, 72.15 and 68.34 seconds. The first uninterrupted
+run exposed unbuffered JSON write overhead; buffering preserves every output byte and reduces
+that overhead. Its 658.55-second wall time is retained in the original report, not promoted as
+the final buffered throughput. These costs do not establish real-time operation, optimized
+release performance or measured physical power.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] Relevant checks returned:
+
+- Eight temporal condition/rest controls, including exact compact reconstruction, corrupted
+  residual-denominator/radius/initial-lift/Gram refusal, canonical framing and remount followed
+  by the same next contact. The reference trajectory ends before the earlier saved cut is remounted.
+- Twenty-nine temporal resident regressions, including complete causal tails, complex
+  quadratures, enclosed convolution/difference, comparison support and producing adjoints.
+- Five public SDK controls covering distinct next recordings after remount, input-clock refusal,
+  output callback failure after contact, no-overwrite publication and checksum-valid malformed
+  clock/lineage/support metadata.
+- Nine acoustic PCM tests: four enclosure/correlation/clipping/clock controls and the five
+  existing exact temporal receiver regressions.
+- The actual source-qualified application/PCM comparison, process-separated byte comparison,
+  and nine cold observer controls (six negative, three positive). The latter include a joint
+  Euclidean-ball counterexample to coordinatewise membership and signed wide-word controls.
+- The public workbench build passed. Formatting checks passed for the new Rust owners and
+  changed codec/support files; `git diff --check` passed.
+
+[established-bounded; process-audit] Reproduction commands live in the [acoustic guide](../../docs/ACOUSTIC_EXPERIMENTS.md).
+Native and SDK controls were run through their Cargo library filters with ignored native tests
+included and one test thread. The 29 temporal regressions use the just-built engine test binary.
+No Lean, CUDA execution or unrelated workspace-wide check is claimed.
+
+## Remaining construction
+
+[open] Bind actual acoustic conditions and generative standing through the admitted native
+owners, inspect useful sound conduct and develop useful recorded English/conversational
+recognition and generation through the same ecology. Complete streaming, interruption/gap
+chronology and measured consumer operation. A restored temporal response and a timed numerical
+sound presentation do not complete AS4–AS5.
